X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:CommunityService
DESCRIPTION: Join our weekly Food Recovery events\, where dedicated volunt
 eers and members gather to make a difference in our community. Each week\
 , participants help collect perfectly good leftover food from Gourmet Din
 ing and transport it to Blanton. There\, the food is repackaged into indi
 vidual microwavable containers and stocked in the food pantry\, providing
  meals for those in need throughout the week. \nTo Participate: RSVP to a
 ttend the event each week. Meet in Blanton Hall Residence Hall Kitchenett
 e in the Communal Area (Tell them you are working with Food Recovery)\, S
 ign in via Event Pass and your set!\nRequirements:\n\nVolunteers must be 
 Food Safe Certified to participate.\nComplete the certification by follow
 ing the step-by-step instructions provided in this link.\nOnce certified\
 , email your certification to foodrecoverynetwork@sgamsu.org to confirm y
 our eligibility to participate.\n\nYour involvement helps reduce food was
 te and insecurity while supporting individuals in our community who are i
 n need. We look forward to your participation!*Please Note: This event en
 d time is dependent on the amount of food given. You can estimate for max
  of hour and a half for recoveries.\n\nHosted by: EATS by Gourmet Dining\
 , Food Recovery Network\, Red Hawk Pantry\n\nAdditional Information can b
 e found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12715230
DTEND:20260915T193000Z
DTSTAMP:20260913T042854Z
DTSTART:20260915T180000Z
GEO:40.859750;-74.199750
LOCATION:Blanton Hall Resident Kitchenette
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Weekly Recovery Initiative
UID:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12715230
URL:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12715230
