SUMMARY:Theater League of Clifton Announces Auditions for “1776”
DESCRIPTION:The Theater League of Clifton will hold auditions for its upcoming production of “1776” on Tuesday\, September 15; Wednesday\, September 16; and Thursday\, September 17\, from 7:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. Callbacks by invitation may also be held Thursday\, September 17. \nAuditions will be held at Living Hope\, 303 Maplewood Ave.\, Clifton\, NJ 07013.\nPerformances will be held November 13\, 14 and 15 at the Wayne Community Center\, 1 Pike Drive\, Wayne\, NJ.\nThe production will be directed by Maren Sugarman. \nWith music and lyrics by Sherman Edwards and a book by Peter Stone\, 1776 dramatizes the struggle within the Second Continental Congress to declare American independence. John Adams\, Benjamin Franklin and Thomas Jefferson attempt to persuade a divided Congress to break with England while political\, regional and personal conflicts threaten to derail the effort. \nThose auditioning should prepare 16 to 32 bars of a song and bring sheet music for the accompanist. A bluetooth speaker will be available if needed. Actors will also be asked to read selections from the script. Please bring a résumé and photo. \nFor information on cast and characters\, please visit https://www.theaterleagueofclifton.com/ or email theaterleagueofclifton@gmail.com or call (973)-928-7668 \nFounded in 2005\, the Theater League of Clifton is a nonprofit community organization dedicated to fostering an appreciation of the arts through theatrical performances while providing quality entertainment for all ages. The Theater League of Clifton welcomes volunteers in all aspects of performance and production. \n1776\nMusic and Lyrics by SHERMAN EDWARDS\nBook by PETER STONE\nBased on a concept by SHERMAN EDWARDS\nOriginal Production Directed by PETER HUNT\nOriginally Produced on the Broadway Stage by STUART OSTROW\n1776 is presented through special arrangement with Music Theatre International (MTI). All authorized performance materials are also supplied by MTI. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/theater-league-of-clifton-announces-auditions-for-1776/2026-09-15/
LOCATION:NJ
CATEGORIES:Art & Culture,Community
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://montclairlocal.news/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/image000000.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Thespaceforart": "https://thespaceforart.com/event/tuesday-night-figure-drawing-open-studio-7/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:thespaceforart
X-SOURCE:The Space For Art
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260915T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260915T213000
DTSTAMP:20260903T004953Z
CREATED:20260903T004953Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260903T004953Z
UID:10269-1789498800-1789507800@thespaceforart.com
SUMMARY:Tuesday Night Figure Drawing - Open Studio
DESCRIPTION:Tuesday Night Figure Drawing – Open Studio \n*Cover art by Ling Chen. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTuesday night at The Space is your invitation to drop in\, find your creative flow\, and practice your drawing skills. \nEach week a different nude model serves as our muse as we pursue creative expression through observation and mark making. We challenge how we see and what we want to say — observing the nuances of the human form\, its moods\, character\, and light — and do our best to capture something in the moment that tells a story. \nThis has become a tight-knit\, supportive community of seekers — artists\, experimenters\, and curious souls drawn together by the shared pursuit of capturing the living human form. Use the time to refine your skills\, experiment with different media\, and deepen your understanding of anatomy\, gesture\, and proportion. Challenge your process if you have one\, or begin to develop one if you don’t. Learn to truly see. \nEach session features a variety of poses\, from quick gesture sketches to longer\, more detailed studies. Whether you’re looking to sharpen your technical abilities\, loosen up your line work\, or simply enjoy the meditative experience of drawing from life\, this open studio is designed to support individual growth in a collaborative atmosphere. All skill levels are welcome – we’ve even had poets drop in and compose verses to the vibe in the room. \nBring your preferred supplies — charcoal\, graphite\, ink\, pastels\, and paint are all welcome. Basic drawing materials are available if you don’t have any\, and the shop has drawing pads and supplies for sale. No formal instruction is provided\, but peer feedback and self-guided exploration are always part of the mix. \nGood music. Good people. See you Tuesday. 7 – 9:30 pm at the Space. \nTickets are set at a capacity of 12\, but we accommodate up to 18 for those paying in cash. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n“The object isn’t to make art\, its to be in that wonderful state which makes art inevitable.” – Robert Henri\n\n\n\n\n\n\n 
URL:https://thespaceforart.com/event/tuesday-night-figure-drawing-open-studio-7/
LOCATION:the Space\, 356 Bloomfield Ave\, Montclair\, New Jersey\, 07042
CATEGORIES:Art,Figure Drawing
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thespaceforart.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/20260820_220438-1-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
