CATEGORIES:Service
CATEGORIES:Medium Size
CATEGORIES:Civics
DESCRIPTION:Join thousands of colleges\, universities\, nonprofits\, busin
 esses\, and community organizations across the country as we celebrate Na
 tional Voter Registration Day—the nation's largest single-day voter regis
 tration effort. This annual\, nonpartisan initiative brings Americans tog
 ether with one shared goal: helping eligible voters get registered\, info
 rmed\, and prepared to participate in our democracy.\nJoin us on Septembe
 r 16 from 12:00–2:00 PM in the Talbott Hall and the Quad at the Bloomfiel
 d College Campus to celebrates this national movement with an afternoon o
 f civic engagement\, entertainment\, and community.\nThis year's event is
  proudly presented in collaboration with the Office of Commuter Life as p
 art of Commuter Life Appreciation Week (CLAW). Together\, we're celebrati
 ng the important role commuter students play in our campus community whil
 e encouraging every Red Hawk to become an informed and engaged participan
 t in our democracy.\nWhether you're registering to vote for the first tim
 e\, updating your voter registration\, or learning more about the upcomin
 g election\, Race to the Ballot is your one-stop destination to get elect
 ion ready.\nThe event will kick off with welcoming remarks from Montclair
  State University President Dr. Jonathan Koppell\, who will officially op
 en the celebration by speaking about the importance of civic participatio
 n and the power of student voices. Throughout the afternoon\, you'll also
  hear from special guest speakers who will share their perspectives on th
 e importance of voting\, civic leadership\, and making a difference in ou
 r communities.\nEnjoy a fun-filled afternoon featuring:\n\nA giant patrio
 tic inflatable obstacle course\nYard games and interactive activities\nIc
 e Cream Truck\nMusic\, giveaways\, and civic swag\nVoter registration ass
 istance and nonpartisan election resources\nInteractive activities hosted
  by campus and community partners\n\nBe sure to stay for the entire event
 ! Students who remain through the closing program will be entered into a 
 raffle for a chance to win an exciting grand prize.\nTogether\, we're joi
 ning a nationwide effort that has helped millions of Americans prepare to
  vote. Race to the Ballot is more than a voter registration event—it's a 
 celebration of civic participation\, community\, and the belief that ever
 y voice has the power to shape the future.\nThe race starts here. The fin
 ish line is the ballot box. Register\, get informed\, and join the moveme
 nt!\n\nHosted by: Bloomfield College Student Government Association (BCSG
 A)\, Civic & Voter Engagement\, Campus Activities at Bloomfield\, Office 
 of Commuter Life\, Office of Student Belonging\n\nAdditional Information 
 can be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12539388
DTEND:20260916T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260913T042854Z
DTSTART:20260916T160000Z
LOCATION:Deacon's Den and Talbott Hall Quad
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:(Bloomfield Campus) National Voter Registration Day: Race to the B
 allot
UID:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12539388
URL:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12539388
X-HOSTS:Office of Student Belonging
