DESCRIPTION:We invite you to attend the Workday Student Town Hall\, a Univ
 ersity-wide conversation about Montclair's transition to Workday Student 
 and what it means for the student experience. This Town Hall is your oppo
 rtunity to hear directly from University leadership\, ask questions about
  the transition to Workday Student\, and learn how you can get involved t
 his fall.\n \nWhat to Expect\n\n\nOpening remarks from President Jonathan
  Koppell\n\n\nA panel of our executive leaders answering the questions ou
 r community has submitted in advance\n\n\nUpdates on upcoming project act
 ivities and how you can participate\n\n\n \nHow do I sign-up\n\n\nComplet
 e our RSVP survey to reserve your seat today! \n\n\nFREE for students\n\n
 \n \nWhere and when?\n\n\nSeptember 23\, 2 - 3pm \n\n\nOn Montclair campu
 s\, join us in-person in Presentation Hall. Doors open at 1:50pm\n\n\nOn 
 Bloomfield campus\, join us for the Livestream in Van Fossan Theater. Doo
 rs open at 1:50pm\n\n\nStay for light refreshments and to continue the co
 nversation at our receptions! 3 - 4pm \n\n\n \nDate and TimeWednesday\, S
 eptember 23\, 2:00 PM - 4:00 PM\nLocation\nAttend In Person Presentation 
 Hall\, College of Communications and Media\, Room 1040\nAttend by Livestr
 eam Van Fossan Theater\, Bloomfield\n\nHosted by: Dean of Students\, Stud
 ent Development and Campus Life\n\nAdditional Information can be found at
 : https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12733446
