DESCRIPTION:**4:45pm** - Shabbat Sha-Blue-Jeans (families with kids 0-2nd 
 grade) in the **YAC**  \n**5:30pm** - Dinner for all families (including J
 LC age families)  \n**6:30pm** - Family Kabbalat Shabbat (for families and
  kids ages 2nd grade and older) in the **sanctuary**  \n  \nDinner in the 
 YAC  \n  \n**RSVP for Dinner:** https://www.google.com/url?q=https://shomr
 ei.org/family&sa=D&source=calendar&ust=1787589009071369&usg=AOvVaw0S2RH-4A
 _Og4Bj9JlGOIhu  \n  \n**Shabbat Sha-Blue-Jeans**  \nJoin Rabbi Uri for a s
 pirited and fun Shabbat service.  \nWear your jeans and come ready to sing
  and dance as we welcome Shabbat together!  \nOpen to all families with ki
 ds in second grade and younger.  \n(Older siblings are welcome.)  \n  \n**
 Shabbat Dinner**   \nFamilies are invited to join for dinner\, stay after 
 Shabbat Sha-Blue-Jeans or come for dinner before the JLC Family Service.  
  \nVoluntary suggested donation of $18 per family to offset costs.  \n  \n
 **Family Kabbalat Shabbat**  \nThis is a highly participatory Kabbalat Sha
 bbat.   \nGeared towards children (2nd- 7th grade) and their parents\, gra
 ndparents\, and caregivers.  \nLed by Rabbi Uri\, Sarah Kamenetsky\, and t
 he students from our JLC (Jewish Learning Center)  \n  \n**Questions?**  \
 nContact the Shomrei office\, (973) 746-5031  \nopen-door@shomrei.org\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260819T212855Z
